Creative Catalyst: Rogue field botanists transduced the raw bio-galvanic microvoltages of rainforest vascular cambium directly into the acoustic keyworks of double reeds to map canopy consciousness.

Phytorāga sounds like a primordial mangrove breathing through a wooden lung. Slithering, microtonal Indian classical meend (glissandi) executed on deep contrabassoons and heckelphones collide with hallucinatory modular synthesis driven by real-time plant bio-conductance. Low, guttural multiphonics mimic the groaning of ancient banyans, while soaring raga structures—unfolding from time-dilated, pulse-free alaaps into frantic, asymmetric jhala climaxes—are submerged in psychedelic tape saturation, moist jungle-cavern reverbs, and narcotic, swirling phytomorphic resonance.

